# Everything here runs on Linux. A checkout on Windows that converts these to
# CRLF produces shell scripts the kernel refuses to start - "bad interpreter:
# /bin/bash^M" - and systemd units that parse strangely. Normalise on commit
# and check out LF regardless of the platform's own preference.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.vhdx binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary

# The licence is a fixed document; a diff of it means something went wrong.
LICENSE -diff

# PowerShell is the exception: it is the one thing here that runs on Windows,
# and the ISE and older hosts want CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
